<x-screen-instructions title="How to use Members">
    <p>The full patron roster — profile, category, ban/watchlist flags, and sensitive fields (ban/watchlist reasons, raw date of birth, staff notes) that only show here, never on the check-in desk.</p>
    <p>A member's edit page has several read-only history tabs — <strong>Attendance</strong>, <strong>Status Changes</strong> (every ban/watchlist/deceased/paperwork flip, logged automatically), <strong>Username Changes</strong> — plus one you can actually add to: <strong>Ban Exceptions</strong>, for admitting a specific banned member to one specific event without lifting the ban.</p>
    <p><strong>Member number</strong> and <strong>username</strong> are locked on this form by design — use the "Rename username" header action for a username change (it's logged), and fix a wrong member number by direct database edit.</p>
    <p>Use the table's bulk action to recategorize several members at once, or the header export to pull a CSV of whatever the table is currently filtered to.</p>
</x-screen-instructions>
